1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,841
Most people save what's left after rent and bills.

2
00:00:04,791 --> 00:00:06,848
That's backwards.

3
00:00:06,848 --> 00:00:09,648
The surplus never shows up.

4
00:00:09,648 --> 00:00:11,132
Flip it.

5
00:00:11,132 --> 00:00:18,072
The day your salary lands, a fixed rupee amount auto-invests — before you can spend it.

6
00:00:18,072 --> 00:00:20,312
Pay yourself first.

7
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:24,765
That's an auto SIP: one standing instruction.

8
00:00:24,765 --> 00:00:28,033
Willpower fails on a Friday night.

9
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:31,015
A standing instruction does not.

10
00:00:31,015 --> 00:00:36,419
You never have to remember, bargain, or skip just this month.

11
00:00:36,419 --> 00:00:42,656
Because you buy on a schedule, not a mood, you average your buys over time.

12
00:00:42,656 --> 00:00:44,036
Quiet.

13
00:00:44,036 --> 00:00:45,664
Automatic.

14
00:00:45,664 --> 00:00:48,723
That's how the habit builds wealth.

15
00:00:48,723 --> 00:00:53,919
This week, set one auto SIP for a number you can live with.

16
00:00:53,919 --> 00:00:56,328
Then leave it alone.

17
00:00:56,328 --> 00:00:59,973
Educational, not investment advice.

